{"id":"title-one-allocations","tier":"OFFICIAL","title":"Federal Title I allocations and California payments to San Francisco Unified","question":"What did federal reporting show for SFUSD, and what amount did California ultimately allocate and pay?","finding":"In 2020–21, ED Data Express reported $12,479,657. California’s revised final allocation was $12,648,592. Its payment schedule shows $13,254,641 had been paid and the state recovered $606,049 by offset. California subsequently reported full payment of the $13,867,852 final 2022–23 allocation and the $16,867,733 final 2023–24 allocation.","how":"The federal series uses one Title I, Part A record per year for NCES district 0634410 (EDFacts data group 797). California’s schedules use district CDS 38684780000000. “State paid” is the schedule’s cumulative gross amount before any separately shown offset. The 2025–26 California final shows $17,572,917 paid. For 2026–27, the preliminary schedule shows $2,552,997 paid against $17,028,122.","limits":"The federal and California releases have different publication dates. A difference between them alone does not establish a missing payment. Blank fields identify years without that source in the comparison. Program-year awards can finance expenses recorded in subsequent district fiscal years.","columns":[{"k":"year","t":"School year","type":"text"},{"k":"amount","t":"Federal allocation series","type":"usd"},{"k":"doc","t":"EDFacts ZIP","type":"link"},{"k":"stateAllocation","t":"California allocation","type":"usd"},{"k":"statePaid","t":"State paid before offsets","type":"usd"},{"k":"offset","t":"Documented recovery by offset","type":"usd"},{"k":"stateDoc","t":"State allocation and payment schedule","type":"link"}],"rows":[{"year":"2015-2016","stateAllocation":11416061,"statePaid":11416061,"stateDoc":{"t":"California payment schedule, 2015-2016","u":"https://web.archive.org/web/20171209082747id_/https://www.cde.ca.gov/fg/fo/r14/documents/title1pa15alloc13.xls"}},{"year":"2016